WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Module 1: SurveyCraft and
the client's workspace.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.251
Before you write a single question,

00:00:07.251 --> 00:00:12.775
settle three things: where the
survey will live, who can see it,

00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:16.055
and how it moves from draft to closed.

00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:17.868
About thirty minutes.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:22.661
SurveyCraft is the survey
platform behind the Mosaic tools.

00:00:22.661 --> 00:00:26.956
It runs everyday surveys you
design yourself, 360 feedback,

00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:30.158
and the Mosaic assessments,
developed by Dr.

00:00:30.158 --> 00:00:33.216
Chris Cancialosi, like the Culture Mosaic.

00:00:33.216 --> 00:00:37.219
This course is about the
first kind, the custom survey.

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:42.387
Every survey belongs to one organization,
which we'll call a workspace.

00:00:42.387 --> 00:00:47.336
People get in through a membership,
and every membership has a role.

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:52.446
Custom surveys and instruments are
built and sent in the same place,

00:00:52.446 --> 00:00:54.684
but they behave very differently.

00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:57.669
In a custom survey, the
questions are yours.

00:00:57.669 --> 00:01:00.314
You write them and you can change them.

00:01:00.314 --> 00:01:05.198
What you get back is charts, comparisons
and exports inside SurveyCraft.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:10.353
There's no benchmark, and you can
duplicate the survey as often as you like.

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:14.491
An instrument's items are locked,
so results stay comparable.

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:16.526
It produces a designed report,

00:01:16.526 --> 00:01:21.478
the Culture Mosaic and Leadership
Mosaic can add to the Mosaic benchmark,

00:01:21.478 --> 00:01:24.327
and each one is bought as a single launch.

00:01:24.327 --> 00:01:28.261
So if a Mosaic tool answers
the client's question, use it.

00:01:28.261 --> 00:01:32.738
Write a custom survey for the
questions the instruments don't ask.

00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:38.862
In the sidebar, the top group is the
platform: Dashboard, Surveys, 360 Feedback,

00:01:38.862 --> 00:01:42.310
Projects, Question Library,
Themes and Purchases.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:48.150
Below it, a shaded Instruments block lists
the Mosaic tools, usually marked to buy.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.824
Bought ones are set up from Purchases.

00:01:50.824 --> 00:01:52.583
Two account types matter.

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:57.509
A buyer account is created when a
client claims something they bought.

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:02.716
It shows only Purchases and the
Instruments block, with no survey builder.

00:02:02.716 --> 00:02:08.134
A licensed workspace has a SurveyCraft
platform license and the full builder.

00:02:08.134 --> 00:02:11.230
The license doesn't
include the instruments,

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:15.029
and licensing a buyer account
switches its builder on.

00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:18.838
Alex wants the pulse in
Northwind's own account.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.385
Choose where you'd build it, and why.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.441
There are four roles, and each
includes everything below it.

00:02:26.441 --> 00:02:29.847
A Viewer reads surveys,
responses and charts,

00:02:29.847 --> 00:02:32.798
but can't export the raw response file.

00:02:32.798 --> 00:02:38.020
An Editor builds, tests, publishes
and sends surveys, and can export.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:41.426
An Admin also manages
who's in the workspace.

00:02:41.426 --> 00:02:43.772
And an Owner can do everything.

00:02:43.772 --> 00:02:46.194
New invitations start as Viewer.

00:02:46.194 --> 00:02:49.146
Give people the least access they need.

00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:52.450
Here's the rule that catches people out.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.563
There's no per-survey sharing.

00:02:54.563 --> 00:02:59.070
Anyone in a workspace, at any
role, can open every survey in it,

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.394
read the answers and export them.

00:03:01.394 --> 00:03:06.746
So never invite a client into a workspace
that holds other clients' surveys.

00:03:06.746 --> 00:03:11.393
The Mosaic team follows the same
rule for its own partner surveys.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:17.309
Every survey has five numbered
steps: Builder, Preview, Distribute,

00:03:17.309 --> 00:03:19.246
Responses and Analytics.

00:03:19.246 --> 00:03:24.251
Then come the optional tabs:
Logic, Theme, Settings and Pulse.

00:03:24.251 --> 00:03:29.014
A 360 survey is sent and read
from its 360 project instead.

00:03:29.014 --> 00:03:35.634
And if you get stuck, Request Assistance
in the builder sends a note to the Mosaic

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:36.037
team.

00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:38.527
A survey starts as a Draft.

00:03:38.527 --> 00:03:40.078
Nobody can answer it.

00:03:40.078 --> 00:03:44.804
Publish makes it Live and creates
its link, but contacts nobody.

00:03:44.804 --> 00:03:50.121
Unpublish takes it back to Draft, but
only while nobody has finished it.

00:03:50.121 --> 00:03:54.994
Close stops the link taking answers
and shows your closed message,

00:03:54.994 --> 00:03:57.431
and everything collected is kept.

00:03:57.431 --> 00:04:00.680
Reopen makes it Live
again on the same link.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:04.077
Archive puts a survey
away with its responses,

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.883
and Restore brings it back as a Draft.

00:04:06.883 --> 00:04:12.643
One detail worth knowing: a Close Date
in Settings stops answers at that time,

00:04:12.643 --> 00:04:17.000
but the status still says Live
until someone presses Close.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.686
You might also see Paused, or Expired
for a bought instrument that missed its

00:04:22.686 --> 00:04:23.867
launch deadline.

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.692
Match each action to what it does.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.695
Projects are folders.

00:04:28.695 --> 00:04:30.903
Use one per client or per year.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:35.033
Duplicate copies a survey with
its questions and settings,

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.881
which is handy for next quarter's pulse.

00:04:37.881 --> 00:04:42.296
But a survey that came from a
purchase, like a Culture Mosaic,

00:04:42.296 --> 00:04:44.860
can't be duplicated into a free one.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.210
To run it again, you buy another.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.286
Time for a quick check before Module 2.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.555
To sum up.

00:04:51.555 --> 00:04:55.936
Custom surveys are yours to
write; instruments are locked,

00:04:55.936 --> 00:04:59.032
reported and bought one launch at a time.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.373
A buyer account has no builder.

00:05:01.373 --> 00:05:06.056
Access is workspace-wide, and
Viewers can read every response.

00:05:06.056 --> 00:05:08.397
And publishing contacts nobody.

00:05:08.397 --> 00:05:13.004
Next, Module 2: designing a
survey that answers the question.

